Source: sekisho
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Naoto Morishima <naoto256@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cargo, rustc (>= 1.95)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/naoto256/sekisho

Package: sekishod
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Description: Identity-Aware Proxy daemon (sekishod)
 Rust-based identity-aware proxy with OIDC/SAML authentication,
 ACME TLS certificate management, and policy-based access control.
 .
 This package contains the proxy daemon (sekishod), its systemd unit,
 the /etc/default/sekishod environment file, and the system user the
 service runs as. Operators can manage it locally or remotely with the
 separately installable sekisho-cli and sekisho-webui packages.

Package: sekisho-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Sekisho management CLI (sekisho-cli)
 JunOS-style interactive shell for managing a local or remote sekishod
 daemon through its HTTPS management API. It can authenticate with an API
 key, or through the local control socket when installed beside the daemon.
 Product-version differences warn; incompatible management API versions
 are rejected at startup.

Package: sekisho-webui
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Description: Sekisho web admin UI (sekisho-webui)
 Read/write web admin UI (axum + Maud + HTMX) for a local or remote
 sekishod management API. Ships its own systemd unit, disabled by default,
 so operators opt in per host. Product-version differences warn;
 incompatible management API versions are rejected at startup.
